Error [jet.FailureDomainNotErrorType]: Explicit failure domain `String (text)` is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:1:15
    |
  1 | fn maybe() -> Int String! { .Ok(1) }
    |               ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: Use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417

Error [jet.PatternTypeMismatch]: Pattern `Ok` doesn't match `Int`
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:6:9
    |
  6 |         .Ok(_) -> { print(true) }
    |         ^^^^^^
 Why: Variant patterns only work on enum values
 Fix: Match a value with a pattern for its type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0305

Error [jet.PatternTypeMismatch]: Pattern `Err` doesn't match `Int`
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:7:9
    |
  7 |         .Err(_) -> { print(false) }
    |         ^^^^^^^
 Why: Variant patterns only work on enum values
 Fix: Match a value with a pattern for its type
